cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "plumbcert: proof-carrying certificates for engineering studies in Lean 4"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andrew
    family-names: Morrissey
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8758-2687"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ASM-21/plumbcert"
url: "https://github.com/ASM-21/plumbcert"
abstract: >-
  Five machine-checked engineering tools in Lean 4 sharing a
  certificate-checking design: an untrusted search procedure emits a small
  certificate, and the Lean kernel re-derives the engineering claim from that
  certificate by computation. Covers worst-case tolerance stack-up,
  dimensional consistency, discrete-time Lyapunov stability, carbon-aware
  load scheduling, and DC power flow N-1 thermal screening. Every checker is
  proved both sound and constructively complete, so a rejection returns the
  specific counterexample. All five build with no dependencies, not even
  mathlib, because carrying physical quantities as scaled integers keeps
  every kernel check within linear integer arithmetic. The methodology is an
  application of certifying algorithms and proof-carrying code to engineering
  study artifacts rather than a new verification technique; see
  docs/RELATED-WORK.md for the prior-art assessment.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - certifying algorithms
  - certificate checking
  - proof-carrying code
  - tolerance analysis
  - dimensional analysis
  - Lyapunov stability
  - carbon-aware computing
  - power systems
  - contingency analysis
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-06"
